@nszzj/dsh-hos-scrcpy README · dsh-hos-scrcpy：**The HarmonyOS provider for DSH** — connects DSH to HarmonyOS devices over `hdc`: see the screen, tap/scroll, press keys, type text, and let the AI do the same.

All UI, AI tools, device/focus state, routing and permission gates **live in core**; this package only knows **how to talk to this device, how to tap it, and how to produce frames**.

> **[中文](./README.md)** | English

@nszzj/dsh-hos-scrcpy README · Install：- Install both, not just the provider (without core this package stays inactive)
- After installing, **fully quit DSH and reopen it** (host-side changes need a restart; client-side only needs a refresh)
- Provider without core: silently inactive because its injection is unsatisfied (by design, not a bug)

@nszzj/dsh-hos-scrcpy README · Development：- Architecture, conventions, what each demo does → [`Dev/doc.md`](Dev/doc.md)
